# Sentinel HOS — Project Context

**Product:** FMCSA 49 CFR Part 395 Hours-of-Service compliance platform (deterministic, auditable). Also referred to as Driver Compliance Watch (DCW).

**Primary app:** `dcw-backend/` — Python 3.12, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, PostgreSQL 16, Redis 7.2. No TypeScript in this repo.

**Architecture reference:** `end-to-end.md` and `dcw-backend/docs/adrs/`. ADRs are binding.

## Current maturity (as of 2026-07-30)

- Modular monolith scaffold + ADRs 001–007 in place
- Geotab ingestion live (DutyStatusLog + LogRecord GPS breadcrumbs); Motive/Samsara adapters are stubs
- Engine rule pack `fmcsa-us-property@1.3.0` with sweeper, replay/backtest, unit tests
- Notifier (Twilio Voice/SMS + alert locks) and HTMX dashboard operational locally
- Driver-day GPS route map (drawer / full page) available when breadcrumbs exist
- WeasyPrint PDF reports and golden fixture suite still planned

## Five-Layer Pipeline

1. **Ingestion** (`dcw-ingestion`) — ARQ cron poller → provider adapter → normalizer → SHA-256 hash → persist
2. **Persistence** — PostgreSQL append-only event store + Redis (cursors, active drivers, pub/sub, alert locks)
3. **Engine** (`dcw-engine`) — Rule pack state machine, deterministic calculators, audit record builder
4. **Notifier** (`dcw-notifier`) — Redis `compliance_alerts` subscriber → alert lock suppression → Twilio Voice/SMS
5. **Dashboard** (`dcw-dashboard`) — FastAPI REST/HTMX queries against Redis + PostgreSQL

## Data Flow Rules

- Telematics feeds enter only through ingestion adapters (Geotab first).
- All provider data maps to `DCWCanonicalHOSLog` before persistence.
- Engine evaluates timelines; every audit record binds `inputs_hash` + `rule_pack_version`.
- Violations publish to Redis pub/sub; notifier handles telephony with idempotent alert locks.
- `canonical_hos_logs`, `gps_breadcrumbs`, and `audit_records` are append-only — never UPDATE or DELETE.

## Dev Commands

Use `dcw-backend/Makefile`: `make dev`, `make worker`, `make test`, `make lint`, `make format`.
See also `make ui`, `make seed-history`, `make backtest-dispatches` for the HTMX timeline workflow.
